**Authorized effects.** {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CategoryProxyTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialProxyTests.removeMaterial on a material referenced by seeded samples is blocked and leaves the store unchanged", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "obligations": ["S22-CONTRACT-SUITES"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}

**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The two store suites become contract suites that any store runs (001 §C 'Contract tests': each library proxy's suite runs against the in-memory store AND SQLite `:memory:`; .spec-md §9). This step moves facts and adds no store; every fact keeps its name and its assertions, except the one named in (1). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs`: `[<AbstractClass>] type MaterialProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshProxy : unit -> MaterialProxy`, a store holding the Built-in catalogue's materials over which no fact removes a sample-referenced material, and `abstract composedProxies : unit -> ReferencingSamples * MaterialProxy`, a store holding the Built-in catalogue's materials whose removal consults the Built-in catalogue's samples. The test-local record `ReferencingSamples = { activeSampleIds : unit -> SampleId list; removeSample : SampleId -> unit }` is the two things the facts do to those samples; a removal that fails, fails the fact. `proxyWithPinned` (step 65) becomes a member over `freshProxy` that pins through `pinMaterialVersion`. These 22 facts become `[<Fact>]` members of the contract: `listMaterials ActiveOnly returns the seeded built-in entries with distinct ids`; `searchMaterials with the empty query matches every seeded entry`; `searchMaterials filters by name fragment case-insensitively`; `searchMaterials dispersion facets partition the library`; `tryGetMaterial hits a known id and misses a minted one`; `resolveVersion hits version 1 of a seed, misses a non-existent version, and misses an unknown id`; `saveMaterial on a new id inserts version 1 active — appears in listing and resolves at v1`; `saveMaterial rejects a blank name as InvalidMaterial and persists nothing`; `KeepCurrent — an identical save on a pinned version leaves exactly version 1 unchanged`; `MutateInPlace — a metadata-only edit of a PINNED version updates version 1 and does NOT mint`; `MutateInPlace — a physics change of an UNPINNED version updates version 1 in place`; `MintNextVersion — a physics change of a PINNED version freezes version 1 and mints version 2`; `latest-active default listing shows one entry per material after a mint, not the frozen history`; `markMaterialInactive hides an entry from the offers yet keeps it resolvable, and markMaterialActive revives it`; `supersedeMaterial behaves as inactive — hidden from offers, present under include-inactive, resolvable by version`; `the lifecycle verbs reject an unknown id with a diagnostic reason`; `removeMaterial on a material referenced by seeded samples is blocked and leaves the store unchanged`; `removeMaterial on a material with a pinned version is blocked with a typed refusal naming the version`; `removeMaterial succeeds when the material is neither sample-referenced nor pinned`; `the referencing lookup is live — removing the referencing sample unblocks the material`; `a MaterialProxy compares by reference (the Elmish-required equality)`; `pinMaterialVersion pins one version, a minted version starts unpinned, and an unknown version is refused`. `removeMaterial on a material referenced by seeded samples is blocked and leaves the store unchanged` asserts that `activeSampleIds ()` still holds `SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId` and `SampleIds.multilayerQwId`, where it asserted that `listSamples ActiveOnly` answered `Ok`. `type MaterialProxyTests () = inherit MaterialProxyContract ()` is the in-memory store: `freshProxy` is `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])`, and `composedProxies` builds `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore ()`, `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (samplesReferencing samples)` and `ReferencingSamples` over that samples store. The facts over no store stay members of `MaterialProxyTests` alone: `a STUB MaterialProxy over the versioned surface exercises every function through its exact signature`; `referencedMaterials covers films, repeated cells, the substrate plate, and the lower half-space`; `referencedMaterialVersions keeps every referenced material version, a repeated cell once`. The values the facts share (`glass`, `otherPhysics`, `glassPhysicsChanged`, `glassRenamed`, `v1Id`, `v2Id`, `minted`) move unchanged into a private module above the classes. (2) `CategoryProxyTests.fs` likewise: `[<AbstractClass>] type CategoryProxyContract ()` declares `abstract stores : unit -> CategoryProxy * MaterialProxy`, a category store holding the Built-in catalogue's categories and a materials store holding its materials, whose entries the category store's removal consults. Its facts are `the real store add/rename/remove of an unreferenced user category round-trips with fixed Guids`; `the real store rejects a duplicate add — a seeded built-in id and a re-added user id`; `the real store rejects a blank-name add and update as InvalidCategory and persists nothing`; `the real store renames a built-in category — built-ins ARE renamable`; `the real store rejects updateCategory and removeCategory on an unknown id`; `the real store refuses to remove a built-in category and leaves the store unchanged`; `the real store blocks removeCategory on a user category a material references and leaves both stores unchanged`; `the referencing lookup is live — removing the referencing material unblocks the category`; the first six use only the category store. `type CategoryProxyTests () = inherit CategoryProxyContract ()` answers `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore (materialsReferencingCategory materials)` over `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore (fun _ -> [])`, which the six facts that built `categoryStore (fun _ -> [])` read alike, because no Built-in material is in a user category. Its own facts are `a CategoryProxy compares by reference (the Elmish-required equality)`; `a STUB CategoryProxy over a fixed category list exercises all four functions through their exact signatures`; `a STUB CategoryProxy surfaces CategoryStillReferenced when a user category is in use`; `a category resolves by id and by name through the list it is given`. (3) The in-memory classes keep the names `MaterialProxyTests` and `CategoryProxyTests`, so every fact keeps its id: xUnit v3 reports an inherited fact under the concrete class that runs it. The abstract contracts hold no discoverable test of their own and get no `ADD_TEST`. Both files keep their compile positions, so no project file changes.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `MaterialProxyContract` and `CategoryProxyContract` MUST be abstract classes holding the store facts, `MaterialProxyTests` and `CategoryProxyTests` MUST be their in-memory subclasses, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged and every MaterialProxyTests and CategoryProxyTests fact under its old id; and build, elevation and the ten s09 invariants MUST pass.
